# No em dashes

Never use em dashes (`—`, `\u2014`, `&mdash;`, `&#8212;`) in user-facing copy, Sanity schema descriptions, or code comments for this project.

Use one of these instead, depending on context:

- Comma: "artists, releases, and initiatives, or discover..."
- Colon: "Afro-gospel and soul-fusion: uplifting music..."
- Period: split into two sentences
- Hyphen `-`: only for compound words or numeric ranges (e.g. `energize-kids.com`, `404: Page not found`)

Before finishing any edit, grep for em dash characters in changed files and replace any matches.
